          %h4#recursion_principle_2 Recursion principle
          %p
            In general, given a type
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weakening+rule"} weakening rule
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            indexed by
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:S^1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            regarded as a constant type family:
          %p The recursion principle for strict circle types states that if:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                We have a type
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
